{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And to his father he sent after this manner</b> — according to this reckoning, and what is the reckoning? Ten donkeys, etc. This is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Genesis 45:23). But it is not correct that it alludes to the reckoning. Rather, it may be that he says 'after this gift,' and its measure is: 'And to his father he sent this gift — ten donkeys,' etc., and the כ is as though superfluous, except that it is the way of the language to speak thus, as in 'and she spoke to him according to these words: thus did your servant to me' (Genesis 39:19). Or he may say: 'And to his father he sent provisions like these provisions that he gave to his brothers' — not to equate them, but just as he gave them provisions for the journey when they went, so he sent his father grain and bread and sustenance for the journey when he would come, and this is the correct interpretation. And he mentioned male donkeys and female donkeys because the burden and the bearer of the burden — he sent him all of it, and it is the custom to send males and females, as his father did (Genesis 32:16)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 45, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:45:03.923775097Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}